			"Message": "fix(deps): Add Rest to workspace members and add missing dependencies\n\n- Remove Rest from workspace exclude array\n- Add Rest to workspace members\n- Add Rest-specific dependencies to workspace:\n  - git2, itertools, par-core (not in workspace)\n  - SWC dependencies: swc_common, swc_ecma_ast, swc_ecma_codegen,\n    swc_ecma_parser, swc_ecma_transforms_base, swc_ecma_transforms_proposal,\n    swc_ecma_transforms_typescript, swc_ecma_visit\n\nAddresses DEP-005: Rest workspace exclusion issue from Part 3 findings",
			"SHA": "7efd868cf40df335e0d761191a4967a9ee8a0b74"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-03-03T11:45:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				113,
				11
			],
			"Message": "chore(Monorepo): Remove debug-wind build profile and streamline profiles\n\nThis commit removes the deprecated `debug-wind` build profile from the Land monorepo build system. The Wind workbench (native Tauri UI with Effect-TS) was previously available as a debug profile but is now consolidated into other profiles.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Build Profile Consolidation\n- Removed `debug-wind` profile from `Maintain/Debug.sh`, `Maintain/Debug/Build.sh`, `Maintain/Debug/Run.sh`, and `Maintain/Profile.sh`\n- Deleted `Maintain/Debug/Wind.sh` script entirely\n- Removed `wind` profile option from `Maintain/Dev-Mountain.sh`\n- Updated profile validation to remove `debug-wind` from known profiles list\n\n### Profile Alias Cleanup\n- Removed `dw` alias (debug-wind) from documentation and scripts\n- Updated documentation tables in `BuildCLIQuickStart.md` and `BuildSystemMigration.md`\n\n### Build Configuration Updates\n- Updated debug profile: `Bundle=false`, `Level=debug` (previously `silent`)\n- Fixed casing in `Dev-Mountain.sh` profile cases (lowercase)\n- Updated `.vscode/land-config.json` to remove wind profile configuration\n\n## Available Profiles\nAfter this change:\n- **Debug**: `debug`, `debug-mountain`, `debug-electron`\n- **Release**: `production`, `release`, `web-browser`\n- **Bundler**: `bundler-preparation`, `swc-bundle`, `oxc-bundle`\n- **Aliases**: `d` (debug), `dm` (debug-mountain), `de` (debug-electron), `p` (production), `r` (release), `w` (web-browser)\n\n## Submodule Updates\n- **Dependency**: Advanced to latest commit with merge from upstream\n- **Element**: Advanced to include naming consistency changes (singular field naming), Mountain thread safety fixes (RwLock for SERVICE_REGISTRY), and Maintain guard disarm mechanism\n\nImpact: Simplifies the build system by removing the underutilized Wind debug profile, reducing maintenance overhead while maintaining debug-mountain as the recommended development profile.",
			"SHA": "1b275fd76d5b6ab9d08a45e26f122c5220e70763"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T13:26:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				114,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Update Mountain submodule to latest commit\n\nThis commit advances the Element submodule pointer to include the recent Mountain backend changes. The update synchronizes the monorepo root with commit d4becf1b23ceb5e8ebda28bab28fe6dd23bf7e3e, which contains the \"save\" functionality implemented in the native backend.\n\nThis is a routine submodule synchronization ensuring the root repository remains aligned with the latest Mountain implementation.",
			"SHA": "6058b40b4d7c5a49f23703c74eeed456f29e655e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-27T13:21:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				114,
				34
			],
			"Message": "feat(Monorepo): Add Mist DNS server and comprehensive security infrastructure\n\nThis commit introduces a defense-in-depth security architecture across the Land ecosystem, along with significant documentation improvements and dependency updates.\n\n## New Element: Mist (DNS Server)\n- Introduces **Mist**, a new DNS server element built on Hickory DNS\n- Creates a secure sandbox resolving `*.editor.land` domains exclusively to localhost\n- Provides `LandDnsResolver` implementing `reqwest::dns::Resolve` for HTTP client integration\n- Implements loopback-only binding, defense-in-depth IP validation, and forward allowlist\n\n## Mountain: TLS Infrastructure & DNS Integration\n- Adds `CertificateManager` for PKI with root CA stored in OS keyring\n- Generates ECDSA P-256 server certificates signed by the CA\n- Implements `ServiceRegistry` for mapping `land://` domain names to local HTTP ports\n- Adds `land://` custom URI scheme handler for webview isolation\n- Starts Hickory DNS server on port 5380 and registers DNS Tauri commands\n- Updates CSP in tauri.conf.json to allow `land:` protocol\n\n## Air: Secured HTTP Clients\n- Creates `Source/HTTP/client.rs` with `secured_client()` functions using custom DNS resolver\n- Routes all HTTP traffic through local DNS server ensuring `*.editor.land` → `127.x.x.x`\n- Updates `Downloader` and `Updates` modules to use secured clients\n\n## Dependencies & Configuration\n- Added `Element/Mist` to workspace members in Cargo.toml\n- Updated tauri to 2.10.2, tokio to 1.49, tonic to 0.14.5, and many others\n- Added hickory-*, rustls, rhai 1.24.0, opentelemetry, and other security dependencies\n- Updated Microsoft and Tauri submodules to latest upstream\n\n## Documentation\n- Created `AtomicFileStructure.md` defining the atomic file organization pattern\n- Enhanced all workflow documentation with Mermaid sequence diagrams and flowcharts\n- Added Known Issues sections to Sky, Vine, and Wind documentation\n- Added Refactoring Priorities documentation with visual diagrams\n- Updated import statements in Wind documentation for semicolon consistency\n- Fixed broken links in various architecture documents\n\n## Cleanup\n- Removed `.astro` build artifacts (content-assets.mjs, content-modules.mjs, content.d.ts, types.d.ts)\n- Updated .lychee.toml with improved link checking configuration\n- Various code cleanup in Element submodules (dead code removal, lint attributes)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: The new `land://` URI scheme requires CSP updates in custom tauri.conf.json configurations.",
			"SHA": "6e32e3a70b9f9256d12f43c2886ddaceb6e6ed12"
		},
